For Wednesday's newsletter, I took a look at how the SPCX IPO impacted Bitcoin and projected what would happen if the same situation played out for the Anthropic IPO.

It mapped to a bottom on Nov 12 right around $69k (and the 200-week moving average).

If last night's bottom holds, it will have played out nearly exactly the same way...

@0xMadaba yes similar analysis, tho I took a look at the difference in cash raises between the two (Ant only raising 59% of the same capital) and applied that, which is why I have the bottom higher than Ben does

@0xMadaba haha same (let us pray)

So @lyft and @Uber are completely overloaded at Newark airport right now. Just hundreds if not thousands of people waiting for rides. I’m in line to get a taxi and it’s wrapping around the corner. Shit is insane. What a fun night. (Way less than half of the line is visible here) https://t.co/iGkCEI1HLy

Lmaooo. Near zero. Everyone is so pissed off. Some people are laughing at the ridiculousness of the situation but it’s also kinda cold. I didn’t really bring a jacket and standing out here for over an hour in slight rain has not been fun. I might get punched if I try to talk to someone about bitcoin or crypto or any book.

@trumanboyes @lyft @Uber I almost did that. But I don’t think it would have helped. Everything is just inundated. And other people were already doing that.

@sunny051488 @lyft @Uber It’s a weeknight after midnight. There’s only so many drivers available. And SOOOOO many people were delayed and diverted to Newark. Just got overrun.

And honestly. I’ve heard some worse horror stories from others traveling tonight. I know someone who was diverted to Philly and is on their way to nyc now in a car from Philly. I also know someone coming from London that was diverted to Boston. Spent a few hours in Boston and then they took off again to land at JFK only to be diverted AGAIN. And where did they get diverted this time? Wait for it … DETROIT. 

So yea. Tonight sucked but it sucked for soooooo many people.

@coinjoined @lyft @Uber It’s usually great but every airport around NYC is fucked today.

